Diagram 2: DAO Governance Operating Model
Title: DAO Control over the Trustless Economy
Objective: To illustrate how DAO members can propose, vote on, and execute changes to the rules of the Economy contract.
Key Actors (Swimlanes):
DAO Member (RepToken Holder)
DAO Governor Contract
Timelock Contract
Economy Contract
User (of the Economy)
Process Flow Specification:
Phase 1: The Governance Loop (Input)
User / DAO Member: Interacts with the platform and identifies a rule in the Economy Contract that needs changing (e.g., "The platform fee is too high").
DAO Member: Earns governance power.
[Action] Calls claimReputationFromEconomy on the RepToken Contract.
[Logic] The RepToken contract reads the member's financial history (earnings/spendings) from the Economy Contract.
[Result] New RepTokens are minted to the member, increasing their voting power.
Phase 2: Proposal Lifecycle
DAO Member: Creates a proposal.
[Action] Calls propose on the DAO Governor.
[Input] The proposal must contain:
Target: The address of the Economy Contract.
Calldata: The exact function call to be executed, e.g., the data for setPlatformFee(150).
Description: A human-readable summary of the change.
[Requirement] The member must hold enough RepTokens to meet the proposalThreshold.
[Result] The proposal is created and enters the (Active) state. The votingPeriod begins.
All DAO Members:
[Action] Call castVote on the DAO Governor (For, Against, or Abstain).
Decision Gateway: Does the vote pass?
[Logic] At the end of the votingPeriod, the DAO Governor checks if the "For" votes have surpassed the quorumFraction and represent a majority.
NO: The proposal state becomes (Defeated). The process ends.
YES: The proposal state becomes (Succeeded).
Phase 3: Execution via Timelock
Anyone:
[Action] Calls queue on the DAO Governor.
[Result] The DAO Governor sends the proposal's Target and Calldata to the Timelock Contract. The proposal is now in the (Queued) state, and the timelockDelay begins.
Wait for timelockDelay to pass.
Anyone:
[Action] Calls execute on the DAO Governor.
[Result] The DAO Governor instructs the Timelock Contract to proceed.
Timelock Contract:
[Action] The Timelock Contract executes the transaction. It calls the Economy Contract with the stored Calldata (setPlatformFee(150)).
Economy Contract:
[Result] The platformFeeBps state variable is updated from its old value to 150. The rule change is now live.
The proposal state is now (Executed).
Key Interactions & Callouts to Highlight on the Diagram:
Draw a "protected shield" icon around the setter functions on the Economy Contract (e.g., setPlatformFee, setAuthorFee).
Draw a single, bold arrow from the Timelock Contract to this shield, labeled "Only Authorized Caller," to emphasize that only the Timelock can change the rules.
Show a feedback loop: Economic activity in the Economy Contract leads to RepTokens, which grant voting power in the DAO Governor, which in turn controls the rules of the Economy Contract.
